The proof shows partnership preserves the side-length multiset and both opposite-angle sums. Fixed ordered side lengths and one opposite-angle sum determine at most one convex quadrilateral up to congruence, so any partner sequence has at most \(4!=24\) congruence classes. Thus an infinite pairwise noncongruent sequence cannot exist.
